{"author":{"affiliation_history":[{"country_code":"US","id":"I95457486","name":"University of California, Berkeley","years":[1978,1979,1982,1983,1984,1985,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025,2026]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I2803209242","name":"University of California System","years":[1983,1994,2007,2012,2014,2017]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I1311060795","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","years":[2013]},{"country_code":"FR","id":"I1294671590","name":"Centre National de la Recherche Scientifique","years":[2001,2004,2007,2009]},{"country_code":"FR","id":"I4387154282","name":"Laboratoire d'Ecologie des Hydrosyst\u00e8mes Naturels et Anthropis\u00e9s","years":[2009]},{"country_code":"FR","id":"I100532134","name":"Lyon 1 Universit\u00e9","years":[2001,2004,2009]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I84218800","name":"University of California, Davis","years":[2009]},{"country_code":"FR","id":"I203339264","name":"Universit\u00e9 de Lyon","years":[2009]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I192389796","name":"Cal Poly Humboldt","years":[2008]},{"country_code":"DE","id":"I54009628","name":"University of Bayreuth","years":[2007]},{"country_code":"DE","id":"I74656192","name":"University of G\u00f6ttingen","years":[2007]},{"country_code":"CH","id":"I202697423","name":"University of Zurich","years":[2007]},{"country_code":"FR","id":"I4387154756","name":"Universit\u00e9 Montpellier 2","years":[2007]},{"country_code":"FR","id":"I19894307","name":"Universit\u00e9 de Montpellier","years":[2007]},{"country_code":"GB","id":"I166337079","name":"Queen Mary University of London","years":[2001]},{"country_code":"GB","id":"I124357947","name":"University of London","years":[2001]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I103635307","name":"University of California, Riverside","years":[2000]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I191859432","name":"National Water Research Institute","years":[1999]},{"country_code":"IL","id":"I16391192","name":"Tel Aviv University","years":[1999]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I142740786","name":"University of Louisville","years":[1972,1975,1976,1977]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I198089087","name":"Ball State University","years":[1976]}],"author_id":"A5043639660","ca_plastic_works_count":3,"ca_works_count":3,"citations_by_year":[{"all":935,"plastic":0,"year":2017},{"all":751,"plastic":0,"year":2018},{"all":887,"plastic":0,"year":2019},{"all":941,"plastic":0,"year":2020},{"all":858,"plastic":0,"year":2021},{"all":748,"plastic":0,"year":2022},{"all":816,"plastic":0,"year":2023},{"all":723,"plastic":0,"year":2024},{"all":635,"plastic":3,"year":2025},{"all":568,"plastic":8,"year":2026}],"cited_by_count":20840,"domain_tags":[],"early_career":false,"first_pub_year":1971,"first_year":2024,"h_index":69,"institution_ids":["I95457486"],"last_year":2026,"m_quotient":1.25,"name":"Vincent H. Resh","orcid":"","plastic_basis":"openalex","plastic_citations":11,"plastic_works_count":3,"primary_affiliations":[{"country_code":"US","id":"I95457486","name":"University of California, Berkeley","source":"openalex_last_known"}],"rising_pct":null,"rising_score":null,"work_count":3,"work_ids":["W4400416707","W4417085695","W7213579226"]},"schema_version":"s3.1","works":[{"abstract":"The lack of systematic approaches and analyses to identify, quantify, and manage the biotic transport of microplastics (MPs) along cross-ecosystem landscapes prevents the current goals of sustainable environmental development from being met. This Perspective proposes a meta-ecosystem framework, which considers organismal and resource flows among ecosystems to shed light on the research and management challenges related to both abiotic and biotic MP transport at landscape levels. We discuss MP transport pathways through species movements and trophic transfers among ecosystems and sub-ecosystems, and highlight these pathways in the mitigation of MP pollution. The integration of biotic pathways across landscapes prioritizes management actions for MP transport using diverse approaches such as wastewater treatment and plastic removal policies to mitigate contamination. In addition, our framework emphasizes the potential sink enhancement of MPs through habitat conservation and enhancement of riparian vegetation. By considering the mechanisms of meta-ecosystem dynamics through the processes of biotic dispersal, accumulation, and the ultimate fate of MPs, advances in the environmental impact assessment and management of MP production can proceed more effectively.","author_count":8,"author_ids":["A5002415995","A5012763496","A5017582449","A5034202916","A5035834394","A5043639660","A5085905281","A5102785802"],"author_institution_ids":["I95457486"],"authors":[{"id":"A5085905281","name":"Ming\u2010Chih Chiu"},{"id":"A5034202916","name":"Sicheng Ao"},{"id":"A5102785802","name":"Chang Ling"},{"id":"A5017582449","name":"Fengzhi He"},{"id":"A5012763496","name":"Qingyi Luo"},{"id":"A5002415995","name":"Zihao Wen"},{"id":"A5035834394","name":"Qinghua Cai"},{"id":"A5043639660","name":"Vincent H. Resh"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":8,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.est.4c04444","domain_tags":["fate_transport_and_sorption","occurrence_and_monitoring","wastewater_and_treatment"],"facet_tags":["matrix:wastewater"],"institution_ids":["I114531698","I19820366","I4210089584","I4210101301","I4210116314","I4210119653","I4210165038","I43545212","I4387152754","I4405286249","I95457486"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"Environmental Science & Technology","last_updated":"2026-11-07T11:25:07.637180","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.est.4c04444","openalex_topics":["T10419","T10447","T10753"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2024-07-08","study_type":"review","title":"Meta-ecosystem Frameworks Can Enhance Control of the Biotic Transport of Microplastics","type":"review","work_id":"W4400416707","year":2024},{"abstract":"","author_count":10,"author_ids":["A5006373071","A5017038190","A5022061329","A5034202916","A5043639660","A5049299022","A5055932703","A5056349018","A5085905281"],"author_institution_ids":["I95457486"],"authors":[{"id":"A5034202916","name":"Sicheng Ao"},{"id":"","name":"Win Cowger"},{"id":"A5043639660","name":"Vincent H. Resh"},{"id":"A5085905281","name":"Ming\u2010Chih Chiu"},{"id":"A5049299022","name":"Dong Zhang"},{"id":"A5055932703","name":"Yuyao Xu"},{"id":"A5056349018","name":"Amit Jagannath Patil"},{"id":"A5022061329","name":"Zhao\u2010Feng Guo"},{"id":"A5006373071","name":"Xin Sun"},{"id":"A5017038190","name":"Yaoyang Xu"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":3,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.watres.2025.125115","domain_tags":["ecotoxicology_and_trophic_transfer","human_exposure_and_health_risk"],"facet_tags":["matrix:marine"],"institution_ids":["I103635307","I19820366","I4210119653","I4210165038","I95457486"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"Water Research","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.watres.2025.125115","openalex_topics":["T10419","T10753","T10765"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2025-12-06","study_type":"article","title":"Biogeographic biases in microplastic ingestion research mask biodiversity and consumption risks across benthic invertebrates","type":"article","work_id":"W4417085695","year":2025},{"abstract":"An understanding of the ecological and evolutionary mechanisms underlying microplastic (MP) ingestions in biological communities is important for mitigating risks to biodiversity and ecosystem health. This study focuses on how evolutionary legacy in community structure can influence their MP ingestion. In a Taiwanese river, we analyzed the phylogenetic structure and MP ingestion in over 30,000 chironomid larvae (Insecta: Diptera: Chironomidae), using over 3 million raw paired-end reads that were generated by DNA metabarcoding high-throughput sequencing from 32 sample sites across the watershed. The results revealed that (1) site-specific variations in MP concentrations were closely associated with the phylogenetic structure of the chironomids present at a site; (2) the type of MP influences their ingestion across sites; and (3) microfibers were the most prevalent type of MP. The link between phylogenetic structure and MP ingestion can guide targeted actions, such as prioritizing pollution control in habitats dominated by high-uptake lineages.","author_count":6,"author_ids":["A5027655739","A5036261635","A5043639660","A5085905281","A5101398261","A5108493254"],"author_institution_ids":["I95457486"],"authors":[{"id":"A5108493254","name":"Chun-Ting Lin"},{"id":"A5027655739","name":"Jhih\u2010Rong Liao"},{"id":"A5101398261","name":"Yucheng Wu"},{"id":"A5036261635","name":"Mei\u2010Hwa Kuo"},{"id":"A5085905281","name":"Ming\u2010Chih Chiu"},{"id":"A5043639660","name":"Vincent H. Resh"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":0,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.hazadv.2026.101583","domain_tags":["ecotoxicology_and_trophic_transfer","human_exposure_and_health_risk"],"facet_tags":["matrix:freshwater"],"institution_ids":["I162838928","I4405257615","I69740276","I95457486"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Journal of Hazardous Materials Advances","last_updated":"2026-11-11T12:16:26.678958","license":"cc-by-nc-nd","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"gold","oa_url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2772416626005772/pdf","openalex_topics":["T10447","T10669","T10753"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2026-09-18","study_type":"article","title":"Evolutionary legacy can shape microplastic ingestion in riverine chironomid insects","type":"article","work_id":"W7213579226","year":2026}]}
